Usage: SET COLORIZE_WARP <number>
  Shifts the colour assignment used by COLORIZE_NICKS and
  COLORIZE_CHANNELS. The default is 0.

  Nick and channel colours are deterministic: each name is hashed
  and the hash selects a palette colour. Sometimes that leaves two
  names you care about in similar colours, or gives a name a colour
  you simply dislike. Setting COLORIZE_WARP to any non-zero value
  folds that value into the hash as salt, which deterministically
  reshuffles every nick and channel to a different colour. Each
  distinct warp value produces its own complete, stable assignment.

  A value of 0 gives the standard assignment. There is no need to
  use large numbers - small values such as 1, 2, 3 already produce
  completely different colour sets; the variable simply accepts any
  integer. The same warp value always yields the same colours, so
  the setting is worth saving once you find an assignment you like.

See Also:
  SET COLORIZE_NICKS
  SET COLORIZE_CHANNELS
